   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to the designation of Southampton Village Ocean Rescue as\nan emergency rescue and first aid squad pursuant to the general municipal law\nand permitting members to display green lights on motor vehicles when engaged\nin emergency operation pursuant to the vehicle and traffic law",
    "basePrintNo": "S8607",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8607-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8607\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to the designation of Southampton Village Ocean\nRescue as an emergency rescue and first aid squad pursuant to the gener-\nal municipal law and permitting members to display green lights on motor\nvehicles when engaged in emergency operation pursuant to the vehicle and\ntraffic law\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to the designation of Southampton Village Ocean Rescue (SVOR) as\nan emergency rescue and first aid squad under section 209-b of the\ngeneral municipal law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the village of Southampton to designate Southamp-\nton Village Ocean Rescue as an emergency rescue and first aid squad, by\nresolution of the village board under section 209-b of the general\nmunicipal law.\n\nSection 2. Once officially designated an emergency rescue and first aid\nsquad under section 209-b of the general municipal law by the Southamp-\nton village board, members of SVOR may display a green light on motor\nvehicles pursuant to paragraph 5 of subdivision 41 of section 375 of the\nvehicle and traffic law.\n\nSection 3. Sets forth an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFounded in 2018, the Southampton Village Ocean Rescue (SVOR) responds to\nemergencies in the ocean and bay, throughout the village of Southampton.\nThey are dedicated to making expeditious and safe water rescues year\nround at all unprotected beaches in Southampton village.\n\nEach month SVOR trains in different locations coordinating with numerous\nemergency agencies to be prepared for a multitude of aquatic emergen-\ncies. They work with the town and village lifeguard agencies as well as\nthe police and fire departments and consistently adapt to new protocols\nto ensure property rescue techniques that best protect the victims and\nrescuers. SVOR rescuers are ocean lifeguard and CPR certified. They\npromote water safety and educate the public the dangers of rip currents.\n\nThis legislation is a special act for the state of New York to recognize\nthe critical life saving functions and services carried out by SVOR by\nauthorizing the village of Southampton to designate SVOR by the adoption\nof a resolution by the village board as an emergency rescue and first\naid squad under section 209-b of the general municipal law. Once desig-\nnated, one green light may be affixed to any motor vehicle owned by a\nSVOR member, a family member or a business enterprise in which such\nmember has a proprietary interest or by which is employed, provided such\nmember has been authorized in writing to affix a green light by the\nchief officer. Such green light may only be displayed hen the member\nis engaged in an emergency operation.\n\nIt should be noted that SVOR is modeled after the successes of the East\nHampton Volunteer Ocean Rescue (EHVOR). In 2020, similar legislation was\nenacted on behalf of EHVOR and they have since been designated by the\ntown of East Hampton as an emergency rescue and first aid squad. This\nlegislation would provide SVOR designation parity with EHVOR.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
